---
// Cookies Policy (EN). General text carried over from the previous
// xanatechnologies.com/en/cookies-policy/ (WordPress); the cookie inventory is
// updated to what this site actually sets (consent cookie + Google Analytics
// via Tag Manager, only after consent). The "Privacy Preferences" button opens
// the consent modal (CookieConsent.astro).
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { COMPANY, LEGAL_ROUTES } from '../i18n/content';
const alternates = { en: LEGAL_ROUTES.en.cookies, es: LEGAL_ROUTES.es.cookies };
---

<Legal
  locale="en"
  title="Cookies Policy"
  description="Which cookies xanatechnologies.com uses, what they are for, and how to accept, reject or manage them."
  alternates={alternates}
  updated="9 September 2026"
>
  <h2>General Information About Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    User trust is important to us, and therefore, at {COMPANY.legalName}, we are committed to
    protecting your privacy. An important part of this is providing you with as much information as
    possible about how we use your personal data, including how we use local data storage and
    similar technologies.
  </p>
  <p>
    Local data storage involves storing different types of data locally on your device through your
    web browser. Data stored locally may include, for example, user settings, information about how
    you navigate our website, which web browser you use, and similar behavior on websites we
    collaborate with. Locally stored data may be used to personalize content and features in our
    services so that your visits are more convenient and meaningful.
  </p>
  <p>
    One method of local data storage is cookies. Cookies are small text files stored on your device
    (PC, mobile phone, or tablet) that allow us to recognize your web browser. Cookies primarily
    contain information about your web browser and any activity that has taken place within it. They
    help us ensure the security and optimal functioning of our website (security and session cookies)
    and collect information about how visitors navigate our website so that our online offerings can
    be made more attractive to users (tracking cookies).
  </p>

  <h2>Additional Information About Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    We use local data storage for a number of purposes, such as: enabling us to provide our
    services; remembering your choices; and measuring and analyzing traffic on our website in order
    to improve our services. More details on these topics are provided below:
  </p>
  <h3>To analyze and improve our services</h3>
  <p>
    We use measurement tools that provide us with statistics and analysis related to our services.
    These tools allow us to recognize the web browser over time and determine whether the user has
    previously visited the website and, if so, how frequently. They give us insight into how many
    unique users we have and how they use our services. We also use the information we collect and
    analyze to develop and improve our services; for example, by identifying which content generates
    high traffic or determining whether a service is functioning optimally.
  </p>
  <h3>To deliver and adapt services to your usage</h3>
  <p>
    Local data storage is required and necessary to allow you to use our services, such as storing
    your cookie preferences so that they are respected on every visit.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies Used on This Website</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies that require consent stay disabled until you accept them. The inventory below reflects
    the cookies this site can set; it will be kept up to date as services are added.
  </p>
  <div class="legal-table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Cookie</th><th>Type</th><th>Provider</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>cc_cookie</td><td>Necessary</td><td>xanatechnologies.com</td><td>Stores your cookie consent choices so the banner is not shown again and your preferences are respected.</td><td>6 months</td></tr>
        <tr><td>_ga</td><td>Analytics</td><td>Google Analytics</td><td>Enables unique visit tracking. The first time a user accesses the website through a browser, this cookie is installed; on later visits with the same browser the user is recognized as the same user. Only if the user changes browsers will they be considered a different user.</td><td>2 years</td></tr>
        <tr><td>_ga_*</td><td>Analytics</td><td>Google Analytics</td><td>Keeps the session state for Google Analytics 4.</td><td>2 years</td></tr>
        <tr><td>_gid</td><td>Analytics</td><td>Google Analytics</td><td>Used to distinguish users.</td><td>24 hours</td></tr>
        <tr><td>_gat</td><td>Analytics</td><td>Google Analytics</td><td>Used to limit request rates, meaning it limits data collection on high-traffic sites.</td><td>1 minute</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Analytics cookies are loaded through Google Tag Manager only after you accept the "Tracking"
    category. The contact form is protected by Cloudflare Turnstile, a strictly necessary anti-bot
    verification that does not set tracking cookies. More information about the processing carried
    out by Google Analytics is available at
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/cookies" rel="noopener" target="_blank">policies.google.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="preferences">Cookie Management on This Website</h2>
  <p>
    You can accept, reject or configure cookies at any time through our privacy preferences panel,
    and later modify or withdraw your consent from the same place:
  </p>
  <p>
    <button type="button" class="cta cta--grad" data-cc="show-preferencesModal">
      <span>Manage cookie preferences</span>
    </button>
  </p>

  <h2>Cookie Management in Your Browser</h2>
  <p>You can also disable cookies or configure your browser to notify you when a cookie is sent.</p>
  <p>
    Your web browser settings typically display a list of all stored cookies to provide you with an
    overview and, if desired, to delete unwanted cookies. You can generally choose to accept the
    storage of cookies from websites you visit or from third parties affiliated with those websites.
    You may also choose to be notified each time a new cookie is stored. Guidance on how to do this
    in different web browsers is provided below. Your web browser typically stores cookies in a
    specific folder on your hard drive so you can review their contents in more detail.
  </p>
  <p>
    However, cookies on the website change frequently, and not all cookies are equally important.
    Therefore, if {COMPANY.legalName} changes the use of tracking cookies, you will be notified via a
    message. Please note that if you disable cookies, you may not be able to enjoy all the features
    of our website.
  </p>
  <p>
    Below is a summary of how locally stored data can be managed in different web browsers. Please
    note that this process may change and that the descriptions provided here may not be up to date.
  </p>

  <h3>Managing Cookies in Google Chrome</h3>
  <p>How to delete cookies:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Go to Settings in your browser menu.</li>
    <li>Click Show advanced settings.</li>
    <li>Click Clear browsing data.</li>
    <li>Select the time range for which you want to delete information from the menu at the top. If you want to delete all cookies in the browser, select All time.</li>
    <li>Check Cookies and other site and plugin data.</li>
    <li>Click Clear browsing data.</li>
    <li>Close the window.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>How to prevent cookies from being stored in your web browser:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Go to Settings in your browser menu.</li>
    <li>Click Show advanced settings and then click Content settings.</li>
    <li>Under Cookies, select your preferred option. If you want to prevent all cookies from being stored, select Do not allow any site to save data.</li>
    <li>Click Done.</li>
    <li>Close the window.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Managing Cookies in Safari</h3>
  <p>How to delete cookies:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Go to Preferences in your browser menu.</li>
    <li>Click the Privacy tab.</li>
    <li>Click Remove All Website Data and then click Remove to delete all cookies.</li>
    <li>Close the window.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>How to prevent cookies from being stored in your web browser:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Go to Preferences in your browser menu.</li>
    <li>Click the Privacy tab.</li>
    <li>Under Cookies and website data, select your preferred option. If you want to prevent all cookies from being stored, select Always block.</li>
    <li>Close the window.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Managing Cookies in Mozilla Firefox</h3>
  <p>How to delete cookies:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Go to Options in your browser menu.</li>
    <li>Click the Privacy tab.</li>
    <li>Click Show Cookies.</li>
    <li>Select the cookies you want to delete and click Remove Selected. Click Remove All if you want to delete all cookies in your web browser.</li>
    <li>Close the window. Any changes you make will be saved automatically.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>How to prevent cookies from being stored in your web browser:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Go to Settings in your browser menu.</li>
    <li>Select the Privacy tab.</li>
    <li>Under History, click Use custom settings for history.</li>
    <li>Select your preferred options under Accept cookies from websites. If you want to prevent all cookies from being stored, uncheck Accept cookies from websites.</li>
    <li>Close the window. Any changes you make will be saved automatically.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Managing Cookies in Microsoft Edge / Internet Explorer</h3>
  <p>How to delete cookies:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Go to Tools (gear icon) in your browser menu.</li>
    <li>Click Internet Options.</li>
    <li>Under the General tab – Browsing history, click Delete.</li>
    <li>Make sure the Cookies and website data option is checked.</li>
    <li>Click Delete.</li>
    <li>Click OK.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>How to prevent cookies from being stored in your web browser:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Go to Tools (gear icon) in your browser menu.</li>
    <li>Click Internet Options and then the Privacy tab.</li>
    <li>Move the slider to the desired level. If you want to prevent all cookies from being stored, select the level Block all cookies.</li>
    <li>Click OK.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Managing Cookies in Opera</h3>
  <p>How to delete cookies:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Go to Settings in your browser menu.</li>
    <li>Select the Privacy &amp; Security tab.</li>
    <li>Click Cookies and then All cookies and site data.</li>
    <li>Select the cookies you want to delete and click Delete. Click Delete All if you want to delete all cookies in your web browser.</li>
    <li>Click Done.</li>
    <li>Close the window.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>How to prevent cookies from being stored in your web browser:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Go to Settings in your browser menu.</li>
    <li>Select the Privacy &amp; Security tab.</li>
    <li>Under Cookies, select your preferred option. If you want to prevent all cookies from being stored, select Do not allow any site to save data.</li>
    <li>Close the window.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Third Parties and Transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Some of these technologies belong to third parties and may, in certain cases, involve
    international data transfers. More information in our
    <a href={LEGAL_ROUTES.en.privacy}>Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact Information</h2>
  <p>
    For greater transparency, if you have any questions regarding the use of local storage on our
    website, please contact us at <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a>,
    indicating in the subject line “Cookie Policy.”
  </p>
</Legal>
